---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Transparency Report #001 — IFFTU">
  <article class="post">
    <div class="post__inner container">
      <header class="post__header">
        <a href="/blog" class="post__back text-mono animate-reveal delay-1">&larr; BACK TO BLOG</a>
        <div class="post__meta animate-reveal delay-2">
          <span class="text-mono">JAN 20, 2025</span>
          <span class="post__sep">/</span>
          <span class="text-mono">12 MIN READ</span>
          <span class="post__sep">/</span>
          <span class="text-mono" style="color: var(--accent);">TRANSPARENCY</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post__title text-display animate-reveal delay-3">TRANSPARENCY<br />REPORT #001</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="post__body animate-reveal delay-4">
        <p class="post__lede text-serif">
          Our first transparency report. Where the money goes, what we're
          working on, and every decision we made this month — explained.
        </p>

        <p>
          Radical transparency isn't a buzzword here. It's a commitment. Every
          month, we publish a full accounting of everything IFFTU does: finances,
          decisions, progress, and failures. This is the first of those reports.
        </p>

        <h2>WHAT WE DID</h2>

        <p>
          January 2025 was our founding month. The majority of our time was
          spent on organizational infrastructure: establishing legal structure,
          setting up development environments, and beginning work on Alexandria.
        </p>

        <p>
          We made 47 commits to the Alexandria repository, established the core
          protocol specification, and began prototyping the peer discovery
          mechanism. All code is available on our public GitHub.
        </p>

        <h2>DECISIONS MADE</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Rust for core infrastructure.</strong> We chose Rust for
          Alexandria's core due to memory safety, performance, and the strength
          of its ecosystem for systems-level networking code.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>AGPL-3.0 license.</strong> We chose the AGPL to ensure that
          any modifications to Alexandria must also be open source, even when
          deployed as a service.
        </p>

        <h2>WHAT'S NEXT</h2>

        <p>
          February will focus on the content-addressed storage layer and initial
          networking primitives. We expect to have a proof-of-concept that can
          share documents between two peers by month's end.
        </p>

        <p>
          We'll also be publishing our first blog post explaining IFFTU's
          mission and the reasoning behind Alexandria.
        </p>

        <div class="post__end">///</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .post {
    padding: calc(6rem + var(--space-xl)) 0 var(--space-xl);
  }

  .post__inner {
    max-width: 740px;
  }

  .post__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .post__back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--gray);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .post__back:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .post__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--gray);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .post__sep {
    color: var(--border);
  }

  .post__title {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  .post__body {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--gray-light);
  }

  .post__lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    color: var(--white);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .post__body p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post__body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-sm);
  }

  .post__body strong {
    color: var(--white);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .post__end {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
